       "content": "# Service Catalogue\n\n## [Consultancy Name] \u2014 Data, Automation & AI Advisory\n\n### *Microsoft 365\u2013centric. Ecosystem-agnostic where it matters.*\n\n---\n\n## Our Positioning\n\nWe help organisations unlock the full value of their data, automate the work that doesn't need humans, and deploy artificial intelligence responsibly \u2014 with Microsoft 365 as the primary operating platform and a pragmatic, best-of-breed approach everywhere else. We are not a Microsoft reseller. We are your independent thinking partner.\n\n---\n\n## 1. DATA\n\n### 1.1 Data Audits & Discovery\n\n| Service | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **M365 Data Footprint Audit** | Comprehensive inventory of data across SharePoint, OneDrive, Teams, Exchange, Viva, and legacy on-prem stores. Maps ownership, sensitivity, retention gaps, and shadow-IT sprawl. |\n| **Data Classification & Sensitivity Review** | Assesses current use of Microsoft Purview labels, DLP policies, and sensitivity labels. Identifies unclassified or misclassified data and recommends a classification taxonomy. |\n| **Cross-Platform Data Audit** | Extends",
       "name": null,
       "reasoning": "The user wants me to write a service catalogue for a Microsoft M365 consultancy. Let me break down the requirements:\n\n1. Focus areas: Data, Data Management, Automation, and A.I.\n2. Service types: Audits, Roadmaps, Advice, and cutting-edge technologies\n3. Primary ecosystem: Microsoft M365\n4. Important nuance: M365 is the primary focus but NOT the only focus - so I need to include services that extend beyond M365 (e.g., Azure, Power Platform, but also other tools, hybrid environments, third-party integrations)\n\nLet me structure this as a professional service catalogue with clear sections, service descriptions, and a logical flow. I'll make it comprehensive but readable.\n\nStructure I'm thinking:\n- Company intro/positioning statement\n- Service areas organized by the four pillars (Data, Data Management, Automation, AI)\n- Within each pillar: Audits, Roadmaps, Advisory, Implementation/Cutting-edge\n- Cross-cutting services (strategy, training, governance)\n- Maybe a \"beyond M365\" section to show breadth\n\nLet me write this in a professional, polished format that could actually be used as a marketing/sales document.",
